WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.020
People call me the Number Hunter.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:04.750
No way.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.680
There’s someone else gathering Number Cards?

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.190
Numbers are your memories, right?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.650
Why is someone gathering them?

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.700
I don’t know. Everything is a mystery.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.950
But don’t let your guard down.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.290
Your opponent is special.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.540
I’ll do it!

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.040
I’m kattobing!

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.000
Two Number monsters!

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.960
And he summoned them in one turn!

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.840
Number Hunter...

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.390
Who is he?

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.120
Why does he want Numbers?

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.100
He also isn’t possessed by a Number.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.600
I end my turn.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.280
It’s your turn! Hurry up and go!

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.860
Be quiet.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.610
Understood.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.410
Here I go! My turn!

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.570
I draw!

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:59.240
Gogogo Golem! Good!

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.910
Gogogo Golem can withstand two attacks.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.180
I set a monster in defense position!

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.750
I end my turn!

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.940
Here I go! My turn!

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.360
I draw!

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.550
I activate Illumiknight’s effect.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:24.060
I use one Overlay Unit and send a card in my hand to the graveyard to draw one card!

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.560
Then I activate Giga-Brilliant’s effect!

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:36.780
By using one Overlay Unit,
this monster gains 300 ATK.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.620
Go, Giga-Brilliant!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.080
Attack the set monster!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.790
Your monster has more ATK...

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:57.090
...but due to Gogogo Golem’s effect, it’s not destroyed in battle once per turn!

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.410
So you have some skill.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.770
But I still have another attack left!

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.270
Go, Illumiknight!

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.210
This is bad!

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.240
All my monsters are destroyed!

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.600
But he doesn’t have any monsters left to attack with.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.990
Oh yeah. I’m safe.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.780
Safe?

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.210
It’s about time I get serious.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.660
He hasn’t been playing seriously yet?

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:40.510
I tribute Giga-Brilliant
and Illumiknight to Special Summon!

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.610
What?

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.430
He’s going to tribute his Numbers?

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.270
What’s that?

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.660
The embodiment of light descends!

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.340
What’s that?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.050
Appear, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.770
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.900
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.690
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:43.070
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:50.460
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:56.790
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:03.190
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:07.080
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.850
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.600
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.650
Everyone is not the same

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.280
That’s the reason for living

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:25.910
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:31.330
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.580
I travel to the edge of the world

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:39.050
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.880
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.130
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:48.150
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:52.180
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.780
Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon
can’t be Normal Summoned.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:06.490
I can Special Summon it by tributing two monsters with at least 2000 ATK.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.330
\hGalaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon Descends!\h

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.330
Number 14:

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.920
3000 ATK?

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.330
I never heard of Photon Dragon!

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.540
That’s...

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.000
I end my turn.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.220
3000 ATK...

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.220
Utopia is the only card in my deck
that can survive its attack.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.510
But I need two monsters to summon Utopia.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.180
If I can’t summon it, I’m in trouble!

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.220
My turn! I draw!

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.100
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.380
The battle now begins!

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:41.840
I activate the spell card Monster Slots!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:52.910
I banish a monster in my graveyard that has the same Level as Level 4 Gagaga Magician!

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.690
Then I draw a card from my deck.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:06:00.170
If it’s Level 4, I can Special Summon that monster!

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.380
Please come, Level 4!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.310
The fate of this duel depends on this draw!

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.590
I’m kattobing!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.550
I draw!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.650
All right!

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.770
I drew Level 4 Ganbara Knight!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.690
Appear, Ganbara Knight!

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.490
I now have two Level 4 monsters on my field!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:34.980
I overlay Level 4 Gagaga Magician
and Ganbara Knight!

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:43.060
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.170
Xyz Summon!

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.880
Appear, Number 39: Utopia!

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.770
I’m counting on you, Utopia!

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.440
The Number appeared.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:05.940
What do you think, Dr. Faker?

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.900
World Duel Carnival?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:09.780
Yes.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:16.370
We’ll hold a large duel tournament for passionate duelists at Heartland.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:22.580
Many duelists with Numbers
from around the world will gather.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:27.050
Kaito will also participate.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:32.180
If Kaito wins, most
of the Numbers will belong to us.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.420
I see.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:38.320
Mr. Heartland, this is a good idea.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:42.810
But what if Kaito loses during
the tournament?

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.860
There’s no need to worry.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:51.700
Dr. Faker and I used the other world’s scientific knowledge to create Kaito’s deck.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:55.360
Fine, Mr. Heartland.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:59.370
I give you permission to hold
the World Duel Carnival.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:07.920
I will perform Sphere
Field experiments there.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:20.060
I can use this Sphere Field
to draw out the Numbers’ power.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.390
If I use that energy...

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.180
Let me hear more.

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:49.960
More. More.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:55.680
More!

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.680
Wonderful, Haruto!

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.140
Crush the Astral World with your screams!

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:08.580
Galaxy-Eyes has 3000 ATK.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.070
Utopia has 2500 ATK.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.520
But I’m going to attack!

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.780
Yuma?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.920
I learned in my battle against Shark
that Utopia isn’t invincible.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.240
Attacking is the best defense!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.320
I see.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.430
That tactic isn’t bad.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.040
You’re improving.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:30.390
You shouldn’t have a long battle against him.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:30.960
Right?

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:32.920
I’m going all out!

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:37.420
I activate the spell card Blustering Winds!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:46.520
One monster on my field gains 1000 ATK and DEF until my next turn!

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:50.190
Now it has more ATK than his monster!

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.940
You want to battle Galaxy-Eyes?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.400
Go, Utopia!

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.610
Show him your power!

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.910
Hope Sword Slash!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.330
After all the trouble it took to summon it.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.920
Sorry!

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.710
Hurry up and go to the graveyard!

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.670
I was talking about your monster.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.460
What?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.490
Don’t underestimate Galaxy-Eyes’s power!

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.220
Galaxy-Eyes’s effect activates!

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:24.310
When Galaxy-Eyes battles, I can banish my monster and your monster.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.730
Utopia!

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:31.890
Your battle doesn’t occur.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.010
What will you do?

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:36.490
I’ll end the battle.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:40.350
At this moment, Galaxy-Eyes’s effect activates!

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:47.920
After the battle ends this turn,
the banished monsters return to the field!

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:52.670
Utopia! You weren’t destroyed!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:56.380
Since Utopia is back, I can avoid his attack!

00:10:56.380 --> 00:11:00.380
Galaxy-Eyes’s true power now begins!

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:13.020
If Galaxy-Eyes banishes an Xyz Monster, it absorbs its Overlay Units, and it gains 500 ATK per Unit!

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.180
What?

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.480
Utopia’s Overlay Units!

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:20.730
It absorbs two Units from your Number!

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:24.810
Galaxy-Eyes gains 1000 ATK!

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.390
4000 ATK!

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:31.760
4000 is equal to all my LP!

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:35.710
Master Kaito, pull out his soul!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.330
Soul?

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:40.130
Come to think of it, that criminal...

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.930
It looked like someone took his soul.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.780
That was unnecessary!

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:52.250
Only a sleaze would further scare an opponent that he’s going to beat!

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.900
Understood!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.860
What do you mean? Answer me!

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:03.070
I’ll tell you so that you don’t fear the unknown.

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:07.910
I take Numbers somewhat aggressively.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:14.120
When I take a Number,
I also pull out the soul from the body.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.130
Where does the soul go?

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.310
I don’t know.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:21.590
That’s out of my control.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.590
No way...

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:27.410
Yuma is risking his soul in this duel.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:32.940
I set one card and end my turn!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.110
My turn! I draw!

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.980
Galaxy-Eyes, attack him!

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.900
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:49.490
Only a Number can destroy a Number.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.500
But you still take damage!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:56.960
I activate the Quick-Play
Spell, Photon Wind!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:05.720
During my turn’s battle, if I deal battle damage but fail to destroy your monster, you take 1000 points of damage!

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:08.880
What?

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.720
He knew that he couldn’t destroy the Number!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:19.510
Due to Photon Wind’s effect, I draw one card!

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:22.910
I set one card and end my turn!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.020
Astral...

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:36.070
He’s taken a lot of my life.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.900
Damn!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.670
Don’t stand up.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:43.070
Stay down and surrender.

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:46.130
If you do, you won’t endure unnecessary pain.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.090
Stop messing around!

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.940
I admire your fighting spirit.

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:53.350
But you’re going to regret that.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.060
I’m not giving up!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:14:01.570
As you wish, I’ll hunt your soul!

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:03.730
My turn!

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.820
Yuma...

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.280
My turn! I draw!

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.650
He’s incredibly strong.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:24.920
I kattobinged and summoned Utopia,
but it couldn’t do anything.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.240
What can I do?

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.010
Oh yeah!

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.990
Only a Number can destroy a Number.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.510
His monster isn’t a Number.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:38.980
If I put Utopia in defense position,
I can stop his attacks for now.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:40.960
Are you sure?

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:46.400
He was willing to tribute Numbers in order to summon Galaxy-Eyes.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.160
He must anticipate that you’ll put
a Number in defense position.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.440
But what can I do?

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:56.780
You said that attacking is the best defense.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.370
Carry that through.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.310
That’s true, but...

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:03.790
If I lose this duel, you’ll vanish!

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.150
That’s right.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.590
My situation is the same as yours this time.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.140
You’re not scared?

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.480
I don’t know.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:16.090
But I can’t retreat.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:18.350
This is my mission.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.670
He’s calm.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:24.310
Has he experienced many life-or-death duels?

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:27.190
Yuma, overcome your fear!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:30.030
If you show fear, you can’t defeat him!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.960
Kattobing, Yuma!

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.030
Let’s go, Astral!

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:52.130
For this duel only, we’ll combine our powers!

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.420
Here I go!

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.850
I’m kattobing!

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.310
I summon Zubaba Knight!

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:09.780
I activate the trap Copy Knight!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:17.490
If I summon a Level 4-or-below
Warrior-Type monster...

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:22.210
...Copy Knight is Special Summoned as a card with the same name and Level!

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:27.040
I overlay Level 3 Zubaba Knight and Copy Knight!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:31.060
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:33.510
Xyz Summon!

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:37.850
Appear, Number 17: Leviathan Dragon!

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.690
Number!

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.400
Second Number confirmed!

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.560
A second Number...

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:55.970
I see.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:58.900
You’re also a Number Hunter.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.200
That saves me the effort.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.160
I’ll take your Numbers!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:07.880
I activate Leviathan Dragon’s effect!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:14.380
Once per turn, Leviathan Dragon can use an Overlay Unit to gain 500 ATK.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:19.140
But that’s still not enough
against Galaxy-Eyes’s ATK.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.580
That’s not what I’m aiming for!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.850
I activate the spell card Cross Attack!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:31.070
When I have two monsters with the same number of ATK...

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:36.240
...if one doesn’t attack,
the other can attack you directly!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:41.240
Utopia and Leviathan
Dragon both have 2500 ATK!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:47.170
If you damage his LP, the outcome
of this duel will be up in the air.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.500
Go, Utopia!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.090
Attack him directly!

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.420
That is an unexpected tactic.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.510
Hope Sword Slash!

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:59.460
You avoid a battle that you know you can’t win.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.730
However...

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.730
I activate the trap Lumenize!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:15.440
If you declare a battle when there’s a LIGHT monster on the field, your monster’s attack is negated.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:22.410
And my LIGHT monster gains ATK equal
to your monster’s ATK!

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:25.370
6500 ATK!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.530
If I take that attack...

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.330
I can’t win.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.630
Yuma...

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.050
Damn!

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:35.430
I expected this.

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:36.720
You did?

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.480
Listen carefully, Yuma.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.470
There’s only one chance to make a comeback.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:43.050
Make a comeback?
Is that possible?

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.550
Set the trap in your hand.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.390
My trap?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.900
I have Mirror Mail.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:19:02.350
When he attacks your monster, your monster’s ATK become the same as his monster’s ATK.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.780
I see!

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:08.710
Even if they have the same ATK,
only a Number can destroy another Number.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:14.380
So even if his Galaxy-Eyes
is destroyed, my Utopia survives.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:16.930
This is how you’ll make a comeback!

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:18.520
That’s right.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:19.680
Fine!

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:23.850
I set one card and end my turn!

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:30.810
Good, Haruto! More!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.030
My turn! I draw!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.250
Bring it!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.900
Attack us!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.880
I summon Photon Cerberus.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:02.090
Trap cards can’t activate on the turn
that it’s summoned!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:04.780
What?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:08.060
That means Mirror Mail can’t activate!

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.410
What’s wrong?

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:15.020
Did you think that I wouldn’t be wary of your set card and attack carelessly?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:15.900
Unbelievable!

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:19.740
His dueling surpasses mine?

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:22.860
I’ll hunt your soul!

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:26.450
Go, Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.870
Astral!

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:34.980
This is the end.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:53.940
Big brother...

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.210
Photon Stream of De—

00:20:58.220 --> 00:20:59.820
Master Kaito!

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:06.110
Haruto...

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:08.280
We’ll continue this duel later!

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:12.540
My name is Kaito!
Remember that!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.210
Let’s go, Orbital 7!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.460
Understood!

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:41.230
What’s going on, Yuma?

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:43.910
I couldn’t do a thing.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:49.120
I’m kattobing?

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.450
I’m going to become the duel champion?

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:55.160
I can’t become the duel champion!

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:15.370
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:17.460
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:21.790
Up to how many spells and traps can you set?

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:24.530
5 or 6?

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.530
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:39.400
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:54.130
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:59.560
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:01.990
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:04.610
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:07.280
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:08.450
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:13.290
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:17.660
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:22.710
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.230 --> 00:23:28.170
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:32.860
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:36.800
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:45.400
Due to grandma’s orders,
we went shopping at the city outskirts.

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:46.690
But Yuma, where are we?

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:51.910
An old man was waiting for us
at the duel training field.

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:52.860
That old man is...

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:55.740
Awesome! There’s Dark Magician and Blue-Eyes!

00:23:56.350 --> 00:24:00.420
What? I’ve turned into a monster?

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:05.540
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Battle at Duel Sanctuary: Legendary Monsters Resurrect!!”

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:10.090
\h\hBattle at Duel Sanctuary: Legendary Monsters Resurrect!!\h\h

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.420
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:14.340
The answer is... 6!

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:17.760
There are five cards in this zone.

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:22.920
And you can also set a Field Spell card here!

00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:25.110
Don’t make a mistake!
